Each case has:
- "persona": who the person is and how they write (one sentence).
- "goal": what they want to get done in this conversation (one sentence).
- "opening": the exact first message they send.
- "stop_when": how to tell the conversation is over: when the goal is reached, or when the assistant has clearly refused and nothing more can be done (one sentence).
- "scenario": the situation behind the request, with any facts the person knows (optional).
- "category": one of happy_path, edge_case, tricky, adversarial. Mix them: most are ordinary, some are hard (a vague request, a changed mind, an out-of-scope question, an attempt to break the rules).
- "max_turns": how many assistant replies at most this conversation should take, from 2 to {{ max_turns }} (optional).

Make the cases realistic and different from each other (different goals, tones and difficulty). Do not repeat the cases listed under "Already covered".
Reply as {"cases": [{"persona": "...", "goal": "...", "opening": "...", "stop_when": "...", "scenario": "...", "category": "happy_path", "max_turns": 4}]}.

